  "worked_solution": "The formula for the derivative of arcsine is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arcsin}\u2061x)=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the chain rule and the formula above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{\u2032}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}[{arcsin}^{5}\u2061(4x)] \\\\  & =5{arcsin}^{4}\u2061(4x)\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}[\\operatorname{arcsin}\u2061(4x)] \\\\  & =5{arcsin}^{4}\u2061(4x)\\cdot [\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-(4x)^{2}}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(4x)] \\\\  & =5{arcsin}^{4}\u2061(4x)\\cdot [\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-(4x)^{2}}}\\cdot 4] \\\\  & =5{arcsin}^{4}\u2061(4x)\\cdot \\frac{4}{\\sqrt{1-16{x}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{20{arcsin}^{4}\u2061(4x)}{\\sqrt{1-16{x}^{2}}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
